            <h2>1. Neutral Dual-Use Technical Protocol Tool</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix is engineered and distributed as a neutral technical utility. In legal taxonomy and architectural design, it operates similarly to standard open developer tools such as <code>curl</code>, <code>wget</code>, <code>tcpdump</code>, and <code>ffmpeg</code>. The software functions neutrally by executing standard HTTP Range requests, parsing text-based manifest files (such as <code>.m3u8</code> and <code>.mpd</code>), and assembling discrete data chunks strictly as specified and directed by the end user.</p>

            <h2>2. No Media Hosting, Relay, or Centralized Storage</h2>
            <p>The developers, maintainers, authors, and hosting infrastructure providers of SaveZonix do NOT host, store, stream, mirror, proxy, or broadcast any video files, audio streams, or multimedia content whatsoever. All media data transferred during the operation of SaveZonix is delivered directly and exclusively between the third-party web servers/CDNs chosen by the user and the user's personal computer. No media traffic passes through or touches any server operated by the authors of SaveZonix.</p>

            <h2>3. Third-Party Platform Disclaimer &amp; Nominative Fair Use</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix is NOT affiliated, associated, authorized, endorsed by, sponsored by, or in any way officially connected with YouTube, Google LLC, Meta Platforms, Inc. (Instagram, Facebook), ByteDance Ltd. (TikTok), X Corp. (Twitter), Vimeo, PixelFlix, Netflix, or any of their parent companies, subsidiaries, or affiliates.</p>
            <p>All brand names, product names, logos, service marks, and registered trademarks displayed or referenced in this software belong exclusively to their respective intellectual property owners. The mention of any third-party company or service is conducted solely under the legal doctrine of <strong>nominative fair use</strong> to accurately describe technical protocol compatibility and interoperability.</p>

            <h2>4. Strictly Prohibited Activities: Copyright Infringement &amp; DRM Circumvention</h2>
